    "text": {
     "en": "The Gupta dynasty began with Chandragupta I around 320 CE. Samudragupta expanded the empire and Chandragupta II, called Vikramaditya, made it prosperous.\nThe empire was divided into provinces and districts with officers. Trade, gold coins and peace helped the economy.\nThe Chinese traveller Fa-Hien visited India in this time and described it as peaceful."
    }
